==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Polevaulter Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Housewife Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
There are two things that define Vaulter Cat: [[Long Distance]] and [[Zombie Killer]]. Her ability to hit her target and the units behind can be a massive help in many instances, namely to prevent peons from reaching the frontline and a possibly frail line of meatshields, thus helping her preservation, but also to reach backliners with at most 499 range, as long as there is a stepping stone. She can also be used to intercept approaching Zombies and [[Slow|Slow]] them before they can get close enough to burrow, so her and other Cats with a similar ability may hope to kill said Zombie, removing the danger of them unburrowing in the wrong place at the wrong time, possibly ruining everything.

She is also the only good damage dealer for Zombies who isn't an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] and has both range and Area Attacks on her side, making her a non-ideal (due to her blindspot), but still great Zombie Killer, at least for a while.

Be aware that this unit has a blindspot and low health, so she needs a very solid defense to work well.

==='''True Form'''===
Housewife Cat can barely be called an improvement. Although she Slows zombies for a second longer (which makes her a more reliable anti-Zombie), she also has increased speed and health as her only other improvements. Her health increases slightly, which gives her a better chance at lasting longer in some occasions. However, her speed is where things get complicated. Due to her nature, a faster speed can easily lead Housewife to run past the meatshields whenever there is an opening in the enemy line, thus putting her in more danger than usual. Although this isn't a big issue and there are benefits to it too, such as getting to the fight earlier or being less vulnerable to the likes of [[Henry]]. The increased health is inconsequential. Unless you wish to unlock her talents, there is little use in getting this True Form over other Super Rares.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Savage Blow]]''' should be your top priority if investing in her Talents, as it increases her DPS by up to 60%. This damage boost is enough to make her outperform similar midrangers such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]]. With this Talent, she serves as a phenomenal counter to [[R.Ost]], who is often featured in stages with limited cash or obnoxious peons; it is in these stages where her cost efficiency and Long Distance piercing truly shine. In [[Procrastinator Parade]], for instance, her solid damage without relying on forming a stack allows her to deal with the early R.Osts quickly and cheaply, while Long Distance ensures she hits any which may be lagging behind. By drastically improving her damage, this Talent allows her to perform well against almost anything she outranges.

'''Attack Buff''' is recommended as a supplement to her already high damage, after boosting her with Catseyes first. '''HP Buff''' is not recommended due to Housewife's reliance on outranging enemies. Whether this Talent is unlocked or not, any moderately strong attack is enough to send her to the sidelines. '''Curse Resist''' and '''Weaken Resist''' aren't relevant and are not worth investing in, as any attack inflicting these effects may kill her outright.

==='''Orb'''===
Housewife relies on her attack stat more than crowd-control capabilities, so most orbs would be meaningless for her. Attack Up vs Zombies is the best orb to use as a result of this.

